---

In a #large bowl{}, mash the @pinto beans{1%15oz can}(drained and rinsed), @taco seasoning{1%teaspoon}, and @salsa{1/2%cup} together until chunky.

Spread 1/4 cup of the bean mixture into half of a @flour tortillas{6%6"}.

Top with @shredded Monterey jack cheese{2/3%cup}, then fold in half.

Repeat until all the tortillas are filled. (It should make 5-6 tacos.)

Add 2 teaspoons of @neutral oil{3%teaspoons}(like avocado oil or vegetable oil) to a #large skillet{} and heat over medium heat for ~{30%seconds}. Swirl it around the pan until the pan is coated.

Place 2-3 tacos in the #skillet{} and cook for ~{4-5%minutes} until golden brown. Flip and continue to cook for ~{2-3%minutes} until crispy.

Remove the tacos from the skillet.

Add an additional teaspoon of oil to the skillet (if necessary) and continue to cook the remaining tacos until crispy.